# __DIST__

__DISPLAY__ harness provider for [openjiuwen](https://pypi.org/project/openjiuwen/). Integration mode: __MODE_LABEL__.

## Install

```bash
pip install openjiuwen
pip install __DIST__          # or: pip install -e . from this directory
```

Installing registers the provider through the `openjiuwen.harness_providers` entry point; no code change in
openjiuwen is needed:

```python
from openjiuwen.harness_providers import available_providers, create_harness, build_harness_context

assert "__PROVIDER__" in available_providers()
harness = create_harness("path/to/agent_template", provider="__PROVIDER__")
context = build_harness_context("path/to/agent_template", provider="__PROVIDER__", host_session_id="session-1")
await harness.start(context)
```

__RUNTIME_NOTE__

## Wheels and the managed runtime

```bash
# pure wheel, CLI installed by the user, one build for every platform
python <skill>/scripts/build_runtime.py --project . --platform macos-arm64 --platform windows-x86_64 --base-url <url>
# optional: bundle the CLI as a fallback, one build per platform
python <skill>/scripts/build_runtime.py --project . --platform macos-arm64 --binary /path/to/__BINARY__ --base-url <url>
```

Both write `dist/runtime-manifest.json`, which a frozen host uses to download, verify (sha256), extract into a
private `site-packages` and append to `sys.path`. A bundled CLI lives under `__PKG__/_bundled/bin/` and is used
only when no CLI is configured or found on `PATH`.

## Develop

```bash
pip install -e ".[test]"
pytest tests/test_harness.py          # fake runtime, no network
pytest tests/test_e2e.py              # the real runtime; skipped when it is not installed
```

See `AGENTS.md` for the verified vendor facts and the invariants this provider keeps.
